Schritt 3: Die GitHub Actions Automatisierung einrichten
Jetzt erstellen wir das Skript, das GitHub anweist, die App zu kompilieren.

Klicke im Repository auf Add file -> Create new file.

Nenne den Pfad exakt: .github/workflows/build-apk.yml

Füge diesen Inhalt ein:

YAML
name: Build Android APK

on:
  push:
    branches: [ main, master ]

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
    - name: Checkout Code
      uses: actions/checkout@v4

    - name: Set up JDK 17
      uses: actions/setup-java@v4
      with:
        distribution: 'temurin'
        java-version: '17'

    - name: Setup Android SDK
      uses: android-actions/setup-android@v3

    - name: Grant execute permission for gradlew
      run: chmod +x gradlew || true

    - name: Build APK with Gradle
      run: |
        if [ -f "./gradlew" ]; then
          ./gradlew assembleRelease
        else
          gradle assembleRelease
        # Fallback falls Gradle-Wrapper fehlt
        fi

    - name: Upload APK Artifact
      uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
      with:
        name: app-release
        path: app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release-unsigned.apk
